Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: core: mark the link off when the host is removed

ufshcd_remove() stops the host controller but leaves the link state as
it was, so ufshcd_hba_exit() still sees an active link and
ufshcd_setup_clocks() skips the clocks marked keep_link_active. On
ufs-qcom that is core_clk_unipro: after an unbind it stays prepared
with nobody to release it, and the next bind takes a new reference.

On SM8250 the unipro RCG runs from gpll0 once clock scaling is off,
which keeps gpll0 and the XO prepared. A Retroid Pocket Flip 2 that
unbinds its idle UFS for s2idle never reached XO shutdown: the cxsd,
aosd and ddr sleep counters stayed at 0.

The link is down once the host is stopped, so say so before the
teardown turns the clocks off.

---
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -10851,6 +10851,8 @@
 	/* disable interrupts */
 	ufshcd_disable_intr(hba, hba->intr_mask);
 	ufshcd_hba_stop(hba);
+	/* Or ufshcd_hba_exit() leaves the keep_link_active clocks prepared. */
+	ufshcd_set_link_off(hba);
 	ufshcd_hba_exit(hba);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ufshcd_remove);
